2026-08-12  Arka Mondal  <arkamondalofficial@gmail.com>

	Version 0.1.1.

	* Makefile: Drop .POSIX:.  It predefines CC and CFLAGS, so the ?=
	assignments below never took effect.
	(CC, CFLAGS, CPPFLAGS, LDFLAGS): Assign with ?=, deferring to the
	environment and the command line.
	(BASE_CFLAGS, BASE_LDFLAGS): New macros.  Carry -std=c99 and the
	-fPIE/-pie pair, which must not be overridden independently.
	(ALL_CFLAGS, ALL_CPPFLAGS, ALL_LDFLAGS): New macros.  Concatenate
	the base macros with the caller's flags, caller last.
	(install): Set destination timestamps from the source with
	touch -r.
	(check-portable): Drop -DVERSION from CPPFLAGS, now in
	ALL_CPPFLAGS.
	* doc/newfile.1: Update the version string.
	* README.md: Document flag precedence.

